is moon knight just another street level  vigilante in the marvel universe just  another superhero no not at all  wondering how his multiple personality  disorder and literal god-given powers  give him an advantage keep watching  mark spector crossed paths with konchu  in his adult life after a botched  operation left him near dead in an  african desert barely making it to a  mystical egyptian tomb spectre passes  away at the feet of the moon god statue  leading to his spirit meaning konchu the  ancient deity saved spectre's life in  exchange for the mercenary becoming his  knight as specter himself recounts in  moon knight volume 9 number 1. this  encounter gives birth to the superhero  called moon knight and fundamentally  changes not only spectre's life but his  brain as well due to the nature of  konchu's powers as a multifaceted  extra-dimensional entity his  interactions with spectre are said to  have contributed to the fracturing of  spectre's psyche in fact it has been  explained on more than one occasion that  spectre's dissociative identity disorder  may have been a direct result of his  mind attempting to match the complex  nature of the god's own persona  furthermore spectre sometimes possesses  the ability to switch between his  personas at will including moon knight  himself which is actually a separate  personality not just a secret identity  the already formidable traits that  spectre possesses due to his military  background are amplified by the powers  of whichever persona is in charge at the  moment  for a time moon knight was able to  harness konchu's powers in the form of  superhuman strength according to the  official handbook of the marvel universe  marvel knights 2005 the fist of kanchu's  physical strength increases under the  light of the moon peaking during nights  with a full moon interestingly moon  knight's strength speed and agility are  all affected by the phase of the moon  full moon half moon waning or waxing  crescent or new moon these fluctuating  power levels are said to be in place  because of specters direct ties to both  the moon and the egyptian god other  guides such as the official handbook of  the marvel universe deluxe edition  number nine established that spectre is  typically capable of bench pressing 450  pounds however he can lift approximately  4 000 pounds when he's operating under a  full moon in recent years however moon  knight has had to deal with the loss of  this useful ability forcing him to push  himself to his physical limits in order  to continue his superhero activities as  spectre himself explained in moon knight  volume 5 9 his super strength was  stripped away from him by a wrathful  kanchu after he went against the gods  orders  as moon knight can likely attest the  cool thing about having a god on your  side is that for as long as they have a  reason to keep you around death will be  less of a final destination for you and  more of a revolving door not that death  ever tends to be permanent in the marvel  universe but still in the case of moon  knight this means that unless konshu  decides to find a new servant spectre is  functionally immortal  in a discussion with his psychiatrist dr  andrea sturman in moon knight volume 9  number 1 spectre confronts the  uncomfortable question of whether or not  he can die with a level of uncertainty  he even recounts that kanchu has  resurrected him not once not twice but  at least three times including when they  met in the egyptian tomb hence on more  than one occasion moon knight has found  himself in a situation where he should  have died but didn't that said konchu  doesn't seem to have any qualms about  reminding spectre that he is disposable  in moon knight volume 5 number 6 during  a vision in which he took the form of  moon knight's horribly disfigured  nemesis bushman he took spectre's life  and brought him back just to prove a  point  while moon knight may be functionally  immortal that doesn't mean his body is  impervious to injury like luke cage in  fact moon knight's battles tend to be  extremely brutal bloody and violent they  almost always end with both him and his  opponents sustaining broken bones  smashed limbs massive bleeding and other  types of physical trauma  rather impressively spectre is able to  bear the extreme pain that comes from  his injuries he has a near superhuman  level of endurance even in the base of  torture from his most sadistic enemies  moon knight's high pain tolerance has  been said to be a combination of his  mental state khanshu's empowerment and  the sheer amount of physical abuse he  experienced during his time in the  military this has led to specter  enduring pain unlike that of any other  street level superhero for instance in  moon knight volume 5 number 6 spectre is  shown to be basically unaffected by  direct crossbow shots from taskmaster  and is able to soundly beat his foe  despite the severity of his injuries six  issues later his crazed former partner  midnight subjects spectre to an inhuman  level of torture his limbs are pinned  against the giant clock that digs into  his back to systematically remove  spectre's vertebrae one bone at a time  moon knight endures his pain long enough  to break free from his restraints he  then defeats his enemy by ripping off  one of the clock's hands and stabbing  him fatally  avengers vol 8 number 33 depicts moon  knight during one of his most powerful  phases in an attempt to stop the  machinations of the hellish ruler  mephisto khanshu decides that it's time  for his earthly avatar to bring about  the age of konchu he imbues spectre with  a host of abilities that the superhero  has never possessed before a fraction of  what konchu himself can do among the  powers that spectre temporarily receives  from the moon god is the ability to  literally control moons and anything  that was made from moon-based materials  this came with the implication that moon  knight could also control many other  celestial bodies as they are mostly made  up of materials of similar cosmic origin  while this power on its own is already  impressive it also granted spectre a  frightening new ability he could  manipulate one of the marvel universe's  most iconic and fearsome weapons a tool  wielded by another god thor's hammer  mjolnir is made out of uru a metal ore  reportedly as old as the universe itself  since urum metal is formed in a dying  star's heart from material that comes  from a primordial moon moon knight's  newfound lunakinesis allows him to  control thor's weapon regardless of his  worthiness spectre demonstrates this  when he makes quick work of the thunder  god by smacking him around with his own  hammer  mark spector shares his mind space with  at least four other main personalities  each with their own unique skill sets  and talents reflective of conscious  multiple aspects combined with his main  persona's own fighting skills and  deductive reasoning spectre maximizes  the talents that each of his personas  brings to the table there is of course  the moon knight persona which is said to  represent kanshu's side as the watcher  of overnight travelers as shown in moon  knight volume 9 number 1. then there's  mr knight a suave sharp dressed  consultant who typically does the  talking there are also two alter egos  that spectre psyche developed in his  youth stephen grant and jake lockley  brant is depicted as a wealthy public  figure and is the persona that finances  moon knight's activities he utilizes and  grows spectre's wealth to allow him to  operate as a costumed vigilante likely  on the other hand is a taxi driver who  wanders around new york and gathers  intel from street level sources for a  brief time in his career spectre was  also able to tap into the abilities of  three iconic avengers sort of as shown  in moon knight volume six number one  spectre developed the personas of  captain america spider-man and wolverine  and would even occasionally have  meetings with them whenever each of the  personas takes control spectre even  equips himself with the appropriate gear  to mimic their iconic movesets  yet another example of a short-lived but  spectacular power in moon knight's  arsenal was shown in avengers volume 8  number 33. after being allowed to tap  into the vast reserves of konchu's might  moon knight gained the ability to absorb  the powers of his opponents via mystical  artifacts however his impressive  absorption abilities also had their  limits moonite first put this ability to  the test in a confrontation with the  iron fist danny rand after subduing iron  fist with a barrage of conscious powered  attacks spectre whips out a divine ankh  which he uses to steal the power of the  immortal dragon residing within rand  using the anks and a bit of necromancy  moon knight easily defeats doctor  strange as well and brazenly takes  control of ghost rider robbie reyes as  spirit of vengeance however the onks  were a virtually no help to moon knight  when he went up against wakanda's  t'challa revealing their limitations as  black panther's powers were granted by  the heart-shaped urby consumed moon  knight could not use the anks to steal  them  [Music]  while moon knight has sported quite a  few different looks over the course of  his costumed career his most iconic  ensemble remains his all-white hooded  suit  and while they may not look like they  offer much in the way of protection  spectre's assorted outfits are actually  designed to be as resistant and durable  as their wearer they're also all white  of course as moon knight prioritizes  shock value and intimidation over the  element of surprise when it comes to  subduing perps spectre's early suits  include kevlar vests as well as a host  of defensive and offensive features  later on moon knight would tweak his  getup to offer even more protection  infusing the design with carbonadium in  the marvel universe carbonadium is  described as a flexible material  comparable to adamantium in terms of  quality and durability you may know  adamantium is the material that coats  wolverine's bones and carbonadium from  its heavy use in x-men villain  omega-red's tentacles moon knight also  wears a long cape that enables him to  catch up drafts and glide across limited  distances as well as metal bracers on  his arms some of moon knight's most  recognizable weapons include his  crescent moon shaped throwing blades and  his adamantium laced bow staff  incredibly the one thing about moon  knight that many may perceive as a  disadvantage has proven to be the  superhero's strongest line of defense  against some of the marvel universe's  greatest minds due to spectre's mental  state the white clad crime fighter has  developed a powerful resistance against  various forms of psychic attacks and  attempts at mind control his mental  resilience also makes it tremendously  difficult for telepathic individuals to  read his mind effectively deterring them  from anticipating his next move or  discerning what his true objectives are  moon knight doesn't take too kindly to  mental invaders in fact as moon knight  volume 9 number 2 shows his mind can be  a very hostile place for unwelcome  visitors while facing off against a  criminal telepath named holly moon  knight was able to overpower his  adversary almost as soon as he invaded  specter himself claims that his direct  interactions with konchu have turned his  mind into poisoned ground the villain  was thoroughly overwhelmed by moon  knight's sheer mental fortitude and was  rendered catatonic after their encounter  while he generally doesn't have access  to this ability moon knight was once  able to wield complete control over his  physical form this includes the ability  to pass right through otherwise  impassable objects as well as being able  to survive in places without an  earth-like atmosphere for extended  periods of time in conan serpent war  number four moon knight finds himself  temporarily time displaced upon his  return to the present day spectre  discovers that he is able to pass  through the glass pane of his residence  transforming into his costumed altar  upon stepping out this power boost which  was granted by khanshu to enable his  servant to complete a series of  complicated tasks is also seen on full  display in avengers volume 8 number 33  as moon knight himself observes he's  able to ride ghost rider's flaming 1969  dodge charger and even battle thor in  outer space without dying  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite marvel characters are  coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]

